1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,087
<i>I couldn't find anything</i>
<i>about Bea's father</i>

2
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:05,130
<i>or her family.</i>

3
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:08,258
[BILLY] <i>I'm not done with Abi.</i>

4
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:11,678
[BEA] <i>Billy said I was a thief.</i>

5
00:00:11,761 --> 00:00:14,389
<i>But she's the original thief herself!</i>

6
00:00:14,472 --> 00:00:16,599
[BILLY]<i> You and Oliver</i>
<i>could've gotten hurt!</i>

7
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:19,060
<i>I won't let that slide.</i>

8
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:21,688
<i>She messed with the wrong person.</i>

9
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,234
[PRECIOUS] <i>Billy.</i>

10
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:28,695
<i>What's that?</i>

11
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:39,414
<i>Enrico's letters?</i>

12
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,709
<i>This is a lot.</i>

13
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:47,630
<i>He didn't forget</i>
<i>about us after all, Auntie.</i>

14
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,553
[DOCTOR] <i>But upon further evaluation</i>
<i>of your condition,</i>

15
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:56,556
<i>you are in an advanced stage</i>
<i>of heart failure.</i>

16
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:59,184
<i>Doc, have you told my family?</i>

17
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:01,186
<i>Ah, not yet.</i>

18
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:03,938
<i>Doc, please.</i>

19
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:05,607
<i>Don't tell them.</i>

20
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:07,650
<i>Your family needs to know</i>

21
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:10,111
<i>that some of your arteries are blocked.</i>

22
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:13,490
<i>Enrico, you will have</i>
<i>to tell them sooner or later.</i>

23
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:15,033
<i>You'll need surgery.</i>

24
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:21,122
[PHONE RINGING]

25
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:23,416
<i>Jordan?</i>

26
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:29,589
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

27
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:30,965
<i>Hello?</i>

28
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:32,258
[JORDAN] <i>Dude?</i>

29
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:34,010
<i>I'm here at your house.</i>

30
00:01:35,386 --> 00:01:37,180
<i>They've recovered some of your things.</i>

31
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:39,474
<i>Would you like to see?</i>

32
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:50,944
[MARIELA] <i>I'm sorry, dear.</i>

33
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:54,614
<i>I've become even more of a burden to you.</i>

34
00:01:54,697 --> 00:01:56,157
<i>You're my mother.</i>

35
00:01:56,741 --> 00:01:57,659
<i>Okay?</i>

36
00:01:57,742 --> 00:01:59,744
<i>You'll never be a burden to me.</i>

37
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,038
<i>You're the only family I have.</i>

38
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:03,414
<i>I'd do anything for you.</i>

39
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:04,791
<i>I'm not.</i>

40
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:06,709
<i>You still have a father.</i>

41
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:10,004
<i>The thing is,</i>
<i>we're not important to him anymore.</i>

42
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:12,382
<i>Is that jerk still alive?</i>

43
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:18,096
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:02:18,179 --> 00:02:24,310
[MONITOR BEEPING]

45
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:25,687
<i>Oh…</i>

46
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:26,688
<i>- Ma?</i>
<i>- Hmm?</i>

47
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:28,398
<i>- Can I take the front seat?</i>
<i>- Nuh-uh.</i>

48
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:29,858
- [MARIELA] <i>You can't.</i>
<i>- Okay then.</i>

49
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,151
<i>You can sit there.</i>

50
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:36,865
[MARIELA GRUNTS]

51
00:02:39,325 --> 00:02:40,410
<i>Okay?</i>

52
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:41,661
[ENGINE STARTS]

53
00:02:41,744 --> 00:02:42,704
<i>- Let's go!</i>
<i>- Ready?</i>

54
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:44,581
<i>- We're ready!</i>
<i>- Where do you want to go?</i>

55
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:45,707
<i>First stop.</i>

56
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:46,666
<i>A convenience store.</i>

57
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:48,585
<i>- Convenience store! Let's go!</i>
<i>- My goodness.</i>

58
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:54,048
[MONITOR BEEPING]

59
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:57,302
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

60
00:03:07,103 --> 00:03:12,358
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

61
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:13,610
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

62
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:14,694
[BILLY] Bea!

63
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:20,575
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:26,664
[GRUNTS]

65
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:28,917
Where do you think you're going?

66
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,793
- Damn you!
- [BEA GRUNTS]

67
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:34,464
[BOTH GRUNTING]

68
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:36,007
[BEA SCREAMING]
Get off me!

69
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:37,467
You witch!

70
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:39,844
[BOTH GRUNTING]

71
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:40,845
[BEA SCREAMS]

72
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:42,555
[THUDS, PANTING]

73
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:43,598
- [KICK LANDS]
- [SCREAMS]

74
00:03:43,681 --> 00:03:44,933
[BILLY PANTING, SCREAMS]

75
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:48,603
What do you want, huh?
Is this what you want?

76
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:52,649
- Damn you, you witch! [SLAP LANDS]
- [BEA GROANING]

77
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:56,027
What more do you want from me, huh?!

78
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:58,279
- Leave us alone!
- [SLAPS LANDING]

79
00:03:58,363 --> 00:04:01,407
Leave us alone! Damn you!

80
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:04,535
Billy! Billy!
[SHRIEKS]

81
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:06,621
[SCREAMS]

82
00:04:06,704 --> 00:04:08,414
[GROANS] Billy!

83
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:09,874
- [PANTING]
- [BEA CHOKING] Billy--

84
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:11,668
[PRECIOUS] Billy! Billy!

85
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:13,920
- That's enough!
- [GUARD] Ma'am, that's enough!

86
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:15,922
- Billy, come on!
- Ma'am, please stop!

87
00:04:16,005 --> 00:04:19,634
- Billy! Billy!
- [SOBBING] Leave us alone!

88
00:04:19,717 --> 00:04:22,053
- [PRECIOUS] Enough, Billy.
- [BEA PANTING]

89
00:04:22,136 --> 00:04:23,221
What, huh?!

90
00:04:24,138 --> 00:04:25,390
You'll pay for this.

91
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:27,183
- You and your mother will pay.
- That's enough!

92
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,227
It'll be jail time for you.

93
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,687
[BILLY] I'll make sure of it.

94
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:37,151
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

95
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:43,950
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:27,744
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

97
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,999
Yo.

98
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:34,876
Boss.

99
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:38,254
Pulled an all-nighter?

100
00:05:38,337 --> 00:05:39,464
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

101
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:42,508
What's that? Still trying to locate
the LoveLine hacker?

102
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:46,554
This is the only way I can help Billy.

103
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:50,516
You know what else you could do?

104
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:54,854
Tell Billy your true feelings.

105
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:57,356
[ROBBIE] There you go! Am I right?

106
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,109
- [ROBBIE LAUGHS]
- Now?

107
00:06:01,194 --> 00:06:03,988
With everything that's going on,
you're telling me to confess?

108
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:05,990
No.

109
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:08,284
No, Robbie.

110
00:06:08,367 --> 00:06:09,827
[INHALES SHARPLY]

111
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,329
I don't want to add to her problems.

112
00:06:11,412 --> 00:06:15,249
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]
- [GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

113
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:18,169
[PHONE RINGING]

114
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:19,837
Dude.

115
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:21,506
[BILLY] <i>Dude.</i>

116
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:22,799
<i>I need your help.</i>

117
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,300
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

118
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:25,551
Okay.

119
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:41,400
[BILLY] I'm Billy Cariño.

120
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:46,072
Mariela Mercado is your mother, correct?

121
00:06:46,155 --> 00:06:48,991
I told you, yes. We've been
going at it since earlier.

122
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:50,201
Where is she?

123
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:52,411
[SIGHS] I told you, I don't know!

124
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:56,415
You've had a record here before,
Marie Beatrice Mercado.

125
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:58,292
But out on bail.

126
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:00,419
[BEA] Exactly. So you know.

127
00:07:00,503 --> 00:07:03,714
You can't just detain me for no reason.

128
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:06,926
Your previous case is a different story.

129
00:07:07,009 --> 00:07:09,971
But this complaint against your mother--

130
00:07:10,054 --> 00:07:12,974
Ma'am, I don't know anything. Okay?

131
00:07:13,057 --> 00:07:14,809
What are you going to do?
I don't know anything.

132
00:07:14,892 --> 00:07:17,061
You'll detain me? You can't do that.

133
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:20,857
That's illegal because you don't
have a warrant.

134
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:21,858
Isn't that right?

135
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:26,279
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

136
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:33,369
[MUSIC BECOMES OMINOUS]

137
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:37,623
[BEA] Can I go now?

138
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:41,836
[POLICE] Yes, Ms. Bea Mercado.
Thank you. You can go now.

139
00:07:45,214 --> 00:07:47,633
Oh, miss, get me away from her.

140
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:50,011
See? She's getting closer.
She'll punch me again.

141
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:51,471
She did this to me.

142
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:52,889
Get her away from me.

143
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:56,642
Why is she still out here?

144
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:59,896
We can't detain her
because there's no evidence

145
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:03,107
that she's an accomplice
in burning your property, Ms. Cariño.

146
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:06,235
I overlooked her being released many times

147
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:09,572
because I respect your due process.

148
00:08:10,406 --> 00:08:13,201
But who knows? Arson might not be
all she'll do next time.

149
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:15,578
She might just murder us.

150
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:17,038
Me?!

151
00:08:17,121 --> 00:08:19,999
How dramatic. I'm not a bad person.
I'm not a murderer.

152
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:21,209
Uh, Ms. Cariño,

153
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:24,962
our search for Mariela Mercado
is still ongoing.

154
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:29,509
Trust that we'll contact you immediately
as soon as we have any news about her.

155
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:31,761
[POLICE] Excuse me.

156
00:08:31,844 --> 00:08:37,058
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

157
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:42,730
Are you sure you want to get out?

158
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:46,734
You might regret it.

159
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:53,407
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

160
00:08:56,744 --> 00:08:58,579
They just let Bea go?!

161
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:03,042
Yes, Auntie Pres.

162
00:09:03,709 --> 00:09:05,545
But don't worry.

163
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:06,712
I'll take care of it.

164
00:09:08,172 --> 00:09:10,049
What? What happened?

165
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:13,094
I'm tired of getting my hopes
up for nothing, Auntie.

166
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:17,557
So I'll put a stop to them myself.

167
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:24,105
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

168
00:09:25,856 --> 00:09:27,191
[PHONE CHIMES]

169
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:40,496
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

170
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,377
[BEA] Ah, sir.

171
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:48,337
Bring me to this hotel.

172
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:53,551
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

173
00:09:57,805 --> 00:10:04,061
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

174
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:32,089
<i>- Billy!</i>
<i>- Hi.</i>

175
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:33,174
<i>- Jordan!</i>
<i>- Hi.</i>

176
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:34,091
<i>Hi.</i>

177
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:36,761
<i>What brings you here?</i>

178
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:38,137
<i>Um…</i>

179
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:41,223
<i>Someone tried to leak</i>
<i>our confidential data.</i>

180
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:44,644
<i>Confidential data?</i>

181
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:45,895
[BILLY] <i>Yes.</i>

182
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:48,105
<i>Transcript of LoveLine calls</i>

183
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:52,902
<i>along with other sensitive information</i>
<i>about our members.</i>

184
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:55,821
<i>But fortunately,</i>

185
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:58,449
<i>we have upgraded</i>
<i>our cybersecurity system,</i>

186
00:10:58,532 --> 00:11:00,743
<i>so we are good.</i>

187
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:02,244
<i>Th-that's good.</i>

188
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:04,705
<i>Should I be worried?</i>

189
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:06,207
<i>No.</i>

190
00:11:08,959 --> 00:11:09,877
[LINE RINGING]

191
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:12,129
Hello, Jordan? Where are you?

192
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:14,423
Summit Bay Suites.

193
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:16,008
We've been here before.

194
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,927
This is where Peter was staying.

195
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:20,554
This can't be a coincidence.

196
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:21,806
Why?

197
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,517
This is where I traced the location

198
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,519
of the person who leaked LoveList's files.

199
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:28,521
Okay. I'm going there.

200
00:11:28,604 --> 00:11:29,605
Okay.

201
00:11:31,565 --> 00:11:37,488
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

202
00:11:53,629 --> 00:12:00,636
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

203
00:12:03,055 --> 00:12:04,014
[PHONE RINGING]

204
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,015
Wilfred.

205
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:09,520
Your and your mom's passports
and birth certificates are ready.

206
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:11,105
Here. Take a look.

207
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:17,570
<i>Okay. Thank you. I'll pick them up later.</i>

208
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:20,281
Wait. You are too excited.

209
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:22,116
Do you have the money yet?

210
00:12:22,199 --> 00:12:25,703
No money, no documents.
You won't get the passport, okay?

211
00:12:25,786 --> 00:12:28,330
<i>I'll get it later, okay?</i>

212
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:29,415
<i>So wait for me.</i>

213
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:38,883
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

214
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:42,136
Ma.

215
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:44,180
Pack your things. We're leaving.

216
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:45,389
Huh?

217
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:47,391
We'll leave now.

218
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:49,602
We're going to Taiwan.
I have a friend there.

219
00:12:49,685 --> 00:12:52,354
They will help us start a new life.

220
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:53,856
Come on! Pack now!

221
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:56,275
So this means

222
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:59,778
that you accept that you lost
to your father's illegitimate daughter?

223
00:13:01,071 --> 00:13:02,823
You're going to run away?

224
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:07,077
Ma, what are you talking about?
I'm doing this for you!

225
00:13:07,786 --> 00:13:10,080
Will we be the losers again, Bea?

226
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:12,708
This is all because of me!
I dragged you into this!

227
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:15,044
No! We haven't lost!

228
00:13:16,086 --> 00:13:19,507
How do we get revenge if we leave?

229
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:24,470
Ma, please,
can we think about revenge later?

230
00:13:24,553 --> 00:13:28,307
If they find you, if they put you in jail,
that's when we lose!

231
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:32,561
Please, let's just pack up and leave.

232
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,281
Dude. Where is she?

233
00:13:45,115 --> 00:13:46,992
- I lost her.
- Huh?!

234
00:13:48,577 --> 00:13:49,995
She suddenly disappeared!

235
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:52,998
I'm sorry. I asked reception,
but they don't want to tell me anything.

236
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:55,167
How did you lose her, Jordan?

237
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:57,378
Sorry.

238
00:13:59,421 --> 00:14:00,631
Wait. Dude.

239
00:14:01,757 --> 00:14:03,050
Is that Peter?

240
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:08,264
I'm at the lobby. Meet me here.

241
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:11,809
No. I'm not going down there.

242
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:13,060
Get up here.

243
00:14:13,143 --> 00:14:15,104
What?! Are you--

244
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:17,648
[WHISPERING] Bea, are you serious?!

245
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:20,609
<i>You better keep your word, Bea.</i>

246
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:25,114
Delete the photo once you get the money,
and then don't ever bother me again!

247
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:28,742
We know it was you, Peter.

248
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:32,162
Remember the leaked files?

249
00:14:33,247 --> 00:14:35,040
It was uploaded from this hotel.

250
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:38,460
[BILLY] You were talking to Bea.

251
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:40,588
Bea Mercado, right?

252
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:44,008
What's your connection to her?

253
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:46,176
Did she force you to steal our files?

254
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:51,181
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,892
Her mother's on the run.

256
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:55,728
And we know she's hiding her here.

257
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:57,563
Just tell us the truth.

258
00:14:58,355 --> 00:15:00,024
It'll make things a lot easier for you.

259
00:15:00,816 --> 00:15:02,651
We heard your conversation with Bea.

260
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:05,404
Is she blackmailing you?

261
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:09,283
[BILLY] You're a lawyer, Peter.

262
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:12,202
You know what you did.

263
00:15:14,204 --> 00:15:18,292
You also know that it's a crime
even if you acted out of coercion.

264
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,879
Now, if you cooperate,
we can handle this properly.

265
00:15:21,962 --> 00:15:26,759
If not, I will have you arrested,
and things will get ugly.

266
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:29,470
Is that what you want?

267
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:36,518
I'll tell you everything.

268
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:44,360
Ma, I'm done packing!

269
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:45,986
What about your things?

270
00:15:47,237 --> 00:15:48,656
That's the only thing you'll bring?

271
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:50,658
[DOORBELL RINGS]

272
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:52,242
Who's that?

273
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:53,410
What else?

274
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:55,996
That's our way out.

275
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,665
Pack your things now, okay?

276
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:05,339
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:16:05,422 --> 00:16:06,966
[DOORBELL RINGING]

278
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:16,141
[DOORBELL RINGING]

279
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:23,565
Ma'am, we need your cooperation!

280
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:24,984
We know you're inside!

281
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:29,405
- Oh! Why?
- Ma. Shh!

282
00:16:29,488 --> 00:16:31,031
- [WHISPERING] Who's that?
- Be quiet!

283
00:16:31,115 --> 00:16:34,243
[WHISPERING] Billy's outside!
She's with the police!

284
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:36,328
Oh no! Oh no!

285
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,038
What are we going to do?!

286
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:41,166
Open it.

287
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:45,838
- What are we going to do?!
- Wait!

288
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:47,381
I'll think! I'll think!

289
00:16:47,464 --> 00:16:50,426
[BREATHING HEAVILY] We've got to get out!

290
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:53,595
[BREATHING HEAVILY] We've got to get out!

291
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:56,974
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

292
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:02,146
[BEA] Sir, wait a minute!
Wait a minute!

293
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:04,106
Mariela Mercado, we have
a warrant for your arrest.

294
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:05,232
Go away!

295
00:17:05,315 --> 00:17:08,694
We are charging you
with qualified trespass to dwelling,

296
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:12,322
frustrated murder, and reckless
imprudence resulting in arson.

297
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:14,074
- Go ahead, cuff her!
- Sir, wait a minute!

298
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:15,242
Wait! Arrest me instead!

299
00:17:15,325 --> 00:17:17,870
Spare my mother!
Take me instead! Please!

300
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:21,248
- You're all animals!
- Ma, no!

301
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:22,416
Cuff her!

302
00:17:22,499 --> 00:17:25,919
Billy, please! Not my mother!
Take me instead!

303
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:27,463
- Billy!
- Cuff her!

304
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:29,840
[BEA] Ma…
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

305
00:17:32,634 --> 00:17:34,803
What? Are you scared?

306
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:36,472
Don't worry.

307
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:41,810
Your daughter will be with you in jail.

308
00:17:43,645 --> 00:17:44,897
[CUFF CLICKS]

309
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:49,568
We'll be the ones messing
with your life this time.

310
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:55,741
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

311
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:16,720
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES,
FADES]

312
00:18:18,555 --> 00:18:19,765
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

313
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:21,391
Dude.

314
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:23,143
Finally!

315
00:18:23,852 --> 00:18:24,770
It's over!

316
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:28,857
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

317
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,275
Damn you!

318
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:32,861
[MARIELA] You are the ones who
should go to prison instead!

319
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:34,571
You should pay!

320
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:38,242
I'll get back at you,
especially you, Billy.

321
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:41,120
I'll get back at you, you bastard!

322
00:18:41,745 --> 00:18:43,956
[OFFICER] That's enough. Take her in.

323
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:50,546
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

324
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:11,942
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

325
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:35,215
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

326
00:19:40,637 --> 00:19:43,765
[PRECIOUS] <i>They're both</i>
<i>in jail now. Thank God.</i>

327
00:19:43,849 --> 00:19:45,767
[BILLY] <i>I have a lot I need to recover.</i>

328
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:47,102
[BEA] <i>No matter what happens,</i>

329
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:48,604
<i>don't tell them</i>

330
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:51,481
<i>that you know</i>
<i>they are Papa's second family.</i>

331
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:52,524
<i>That's the truth.</i>

332
00:19:52,608 --> 00:19:56,278
<i>It'll just prove that you're</i>
<i>going after Papa's illegitimate child.</i>

333
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:58,530
<i>And Oliver will stay there.</i>

334
00:19:58,614 --> 00:19:59,531
<i>As well as Dad.</i>

335
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:01,742
<i>You're letting your father</i>
<i>live here with us?</i>

336
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:02,826
<i>Are you sure about this?</i>

337
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,161
<i>Your father</i>

338
00:20:04,953 --> 00:20:07,873
<i>is asking about the fire.</i>

339
00:20:07,956 --> 00:20:09,875
<i>He wants to know what really happened.</i>

340
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,044
[BEA] <i>I will do</i>
<i>everything possible, Ma.</i>

341
00:20:12,127 --> 00:20:14,463
<i>I will do everything I can</i>
<i>to get you out of here.</i>

342
00:20:14,546 --> 00:20:15,881
<i>Not just me.</i>

343
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:17,299
<i>Both of us.</i>

344
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:19,176
<i>I found these.</i>

345
00:20:19,259 --> 00:20:20,928
<i>I've read all of them too.</i>

346
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:24,014
<i>Would it be okay</i>
<i>if I asked for a hug?</i>

347
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:27,935
<i>I don't know if Billy will ever</i>
<i>be able to forgive me</i>

348
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:29,186
<i>for what I'm about to tell her.</i>

349
00:20:29,269 --> 00:20:30,103
FIRE BURNS DOWN HOME

350
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:31,605
<i>I know this is too much.</i>

351
00:20:31,688 --> 00:20:33,941
<i>But she needs to know the truth.</i>

352
00:20:34,024 --> 00:20:35,734
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

353
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:40,697
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
